# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SCHOLAR AI - ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to a new file named '.env' and fill in your keys.

# ── REQUIRED: GOOGLE GEMINI API CONFIGURATION ────────────────────────────────
# Get your API key from Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com)
# You can specify a single key or a list of multiple keys separated by commas (e.g. key1,key2,key3).
# If a key exhausts its quota or rate limits, the application will automatically failover/switch to the next key.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-google-gemini-api-key-here

# ── OPTIONAL: FALLBACK PROVIDERS CONFIGURATION (For Free Alternative Models) ────
# Specify backup keys to fall back to free models if Gemini keys are exhausted.
# Supports comma-separated list of multiple keys for rotation.
GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key-here
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your-openrouter-api-key-here

# ── OPTIONAL: SUPABASE STORAGE CONFIGURATION (For Persistent Cloud Deploy) ────
# Leave these commented out to run in standard Local Offline Mode (data stored locally).
# Uncomment and fill them to run in Cloud Mode (Supabase Auth, Database, Storage).
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key-here

# ── OPTIONAL: SMTP EMAIL CONFIGURATION (For Real Verification Emails) ────────
# Leave these commented out to print verification codes directly in the terminal/app.
# Uncomment and configure with your SMTP settings (e.g. Gmail App Passwords) to send real emails.
SMTP_SERVER=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=capabltechies@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your-email-app-password
SMTP_FROM=capabltechies@gmail.com
